WEBVTT

00:27.830 --> 00:31.540
<b>FATAL CRASHES</b>

00:27.830 --> 00:31.540
<b>IN THIS AREA</b>

00:41.500 --> 00:48.960
<b>FATAL CRASHES</b>

00:41.500 --> 00:48.960
<b>IN THIS AREA</b>

00:43.330 --> 00:46.460
Even if you try to hide in a bathroom...

00:49.790 --> 00:50.880
I will...

00:52.000 --> 00:53.040
...find you.

02:25.460 --> 02:28.460
<b>REIO UNIVERSITY</b>

02:25.460 --> 02:28.460
<b>REIO UNIVERSITY</b>

02:25.460 --> 02:28.460
<b>WELCOME ASSEMBLY</b>

02:28.460 --> 02:31.420
<b>REIO UNIVERSITY</b>

02:28.460 --> 02:31.420
<b>WELCOME ASSEMBLY</b>

02:31.960 --> 02:37.380
Here to present the freshman welcome address...
is freshman class representative Keitaro Gentoga.

02:39.130 --> 02:42.330
The hightest scorer on the entrance exam
gets to give the speech, right?

02:42.500 --> 02:44.130
Whoa!

02:58.290 --> 03:01.380
I hate the supernatural.

02:58.330 --> 03:01.880
<b>I HATE THE SUPERNATURAL</b>

03:08.880 --> 03:11.500
Should've known it'd end up cursed.

03:13.170 --> 03:16.170
I'm so sorry! I shouldn't have badgered you into it...

03:14.420 --> 03:16.500
<b>Keitaro's Longtime Friend</b>

03:14.420 --> 03:16.500
<b>Eiko Hozuki</b>

03:16.630 --> 03:20.080
It's fine, Eiko. It's not your fault.

03:21.210 --> 03:24.750
Literally every photo taken of me turns out like that.

03:27.250 --> 03:29.710
Spirits are naturally drawn to me.

03:30.710 --> 03:33.790
Back in middle school,
I got tangled up with a nasty spirit,

03:34.880 --> 03:37.380
and a good friend got dragged into it, too.

03:38.330 --> 03:39.710
For the next two years,

03:39.790 --> 03:43.790
I was so afraid of getting anyone else hurt,
that I refused to leave my room.

03:44.670 --> 03:47.710
But with the help of my old friend Eiko,
my family, and the people around me,

03:48.290 --> 03:53.670
last year, I started trying to live a normal life in society.

03:55.250 --> 03:57.540
I even managed to catch up with school.

03:58.290 --> 04:01.670
Oh, yeah, did you hear back from the tutoring place?

04:01.880 --> 04:05.750
You mean the one you recommended? I got the job.

04:05.960 --> 04:10.710
Yay! I got the idea
for Private Tutor Square from my cousin!

04:11.000 --> 04:12.080
She gets tutoring there.

04:12.080 --> 04:15.750
Really? Is that why you suggested it to me?

04:17.290 --> 04:20.420
<b>REIO UNIVERSITY</b>

04:17.290 --> 04:20.420
<b>WELCOME ASSEMBLY</b>

04:17.830 --> 04:20.420
Freshman class rep and a tutor.

04:20.830 --> 04:23.500
Both are huge steps forward
to getting your normal life back.

04:24.630 --> 04:25.630
Plus...

04:26.750 --> 04:29.130
We get to go to the same school again!

04:29.540 --> 04:31.880
It's gonna be so great!

04:32.710 --> 04:33.500
Yeah...

04:36.080 --> 04:40.250
All those years being a recluse
have really crippled my social skills.

04:40.330 --> 04:45.290
<b>Private Tutor Square</b>

04:41.040 --> 04:45.210
Not to mention all the spirits drawn to me.
My work's cut out for me.

04:46.380 --> 04:49.040
But I'm going to live a normal life!

04:49.040 --> 04:51.630
Okay, this is the girl you're in charge of.

04:51.630 --> 04:52.540
Y-yes, sir!

04:52.750 --> 04:54.790
You can relax a little, you know...

04:54.960 --> 04:55.540
Yes, sir...

04:55.710 --> 05:00.670
I don't blame you, though.
This girl is our most promising student.

04:59.250 --> 05:01.000
<b>Yayoi Hozuki:</b>

04:59.250 --> 05:01.000
<b>3rd Grade</b>

04:59.250 --> 05:01.000
<b>Scored well above average in 4 subjects</b>

04:59.250 --> 05:01.000
<b>Potential Middle Schools:</b>

05:00.920 --> 05:02.250
She's a real prodigy.

05:01.000 --> 05:02.500
<b>Yayoi Hozuki:</b>

05:01.000 --> 05:02.500
<b>3rd Grade</b>

05:01.000 --> 05:02.500
<b>Scored well above average in 4 subjects</b>

05:04.790 --> 05:08.000
Come out, come out,

05:08.500 --> 05:10.000
come out...

05:10.920 --> 05:14.080
With you being class rep,
they specifically wanted you as her tutor.

05:14.460 --> 05:15.540
We know you'll do great.

05:15.750 --> 05:17.170
<b>HOZUKI</b>

05:17.420 --> 05:20.460
I thought the name was just a coincidence...

05:22.830 --> 05:24.460
Kei-kun? What are you doing here?

05:24.580 --> 05:28.420
Uh, I'm here for my job. Did I get the place wrong?

05:28.880 --> 05:30.670
You don't have a little sister, do you?

05:30.830 --> 05:35.210
Oh! I have a little cousin,
and she's been living with me for the past year!

05:36.460 --> 05:38.790
Wait, so she's the one I'm here for?

05:38.040 --> 05:42.540
<b>Yayoi Hozuki:</b>

05:38.040 --> 05:42.540
<b>3rd Grade</b>

05:38.040 --> 05:42.540
<b>Scored well above average in 4 subjects</b>

05:38.960 --> 05:42.170
That must be it! What a crazy coincidence!

05:42.540 --> 05:45.500
I can't believe you're going to be tutoring her, Kei-kun!

05:45.960 --> 05:48.880
Hey, your tutor is here!

05:56.040 --> 05:59.460
Eiko! What kind of creature are you living with?!

05:59.580 --> 06:01.420
Huh? What creature?

06:01.790 --> 06:03.880
That's my little cousin, Yayoi Hozuki.

06:08.460 --> 06:10.830
She has two pupils in each eye...

06:12.670 --> 06:15.500
There's a real big one on your right hand.

06:17.750 --> 06:19.790
Sh-she can see it!

06:21.580 --> 06:22.790
Whoa...

06:23.670 --> 06:26.170
Is this horrible feeling...

06:27.130 --> 06:28.380
...coming from THAT?

06:30.460 --> 06:32.790
You... You need to get away from that plushie!

06:36.210 --> 06:37.210
Sorry about him.

06:37.500 --> 06:41.460
I'll choke him out for you.

06:42.420 --> 06:45.330
There's no doubt about it.
She can see spirits, just like me.

06:45.790 --> 06:48.460
She might be even more sensitive than me, actually!

06:48.920 --> 06:50.540
Kei-kun, what's wrong?

06:52.540 --> 06:53.670
Right...

06:57.540 --> 06:58.540
C'mon, me!

07:00.920 --> 07:05.420
My name's Keitaro Gentoga.
I'm going to be your home tutor.

07:05.750 --> 07:06.540
Nice to meet you.

07:07.830 --> 07:09.330
Keitaro-sensei.

07:09.880 --> 07:11.630
Let's go somewhere haunted.

07:11.830 --> 07:12.500
What?!

07:13.630 --> 07:16.330
Hold on! I'm here to help you study!

07:16.330 --> 07:17.210
I know.

07:17.710 --> 07:23.040
But spirits really like you,
so we'll probably see one if we go.

07:23.500 --> 07:26.000
She's definitely not human!

07:26.750 --> 07:29.040
No, we really should study instead!

07:29.040 --> 07:30.540
Hello, Private Tutor Square?

07:30.540 --> 07:34.920
Keitaro-sensei just asked cute, little me:
"Mwehehe, what kinda panties you wearin', little girl?"

07:35.830 --> 07:37.210
I didn't! I swear I didn't!

07:37.380 --> 07:38.750
Eiko, you've gotta help me!

07:38.920 --> 07:40.500
Ready to roll here!

07:40.500 --> 07:41.710
Come on!

07:42.790 --> 07:44.080
Let's gooo...

07:44.080 --> 07:45.170
...oost!

07:48.130 --> 07:50.000
This is not what I signed up for!

07:50.290 --> 07:51.960
I wanna bail out and run!

07:53.710 --> 07:55.580
Eiko, what the hell?!

07:55.670 --> 07:57.830
You know this isn't safe!

07:58.130 --> 08:01.540
Yayoi-chan is always begging me to go,

08:01.960 --> 08:04.420
but I always say no.

08:04.540 --> 08:05.460
So say no again!

08:05.630 --> 08:09.170
But I figured we'd be fine
if someone as experienced as you came along!

08:09.710 --> 08:13.080
But I can only sense them, not see them,
and I definitely can't exorcise them!

08:13.880 --> 08:16.710
Well, if things get really bad, we'll just leave!

08:16.960 --> 08:19.960
Maybe this'll just end up being a fun little drive.

08:25.830 --> 08:28.960
So... I'm already getting mad chills.

08:29.130 --> 08:31.880
What? But we still have a whole kilometer to go.

08:32.500 --> 08:36.080
If I can feel it from this far out,
we should probably turn around now.

08:36.170 --> 08:38.540
You a scaredy-cat, Keitaro?

08:38.540 --> 08:39.790
What happened to "sensei"?!

08:40.580 --> 08:41.380
Eiko!

08:43.290 --> 08:44.250
It's fine.

08:48.880 --> 08:51.250
What the hell is wrong with this girl?!

08:58.500 --> 08:59.670
Here we are!

09:00.170 --> 09:02.170
The Haunted Phone Booth of H City!

09:02.960 --> 09:05.830
I haven't told you the story behind this place, have I?

09:06.080 --> 09:07.330
I don't want to hear it...

09:07.670 --> 09:12.040
Apparently, it's haunted by the ghost of a young woman.

09:12.040 --> 09:14.040
I just told you, I don't want to hear it!

09:14.040 --> 09:16.380
Keep it up. You're setting the mood.

09:16.670 --> 09:23.540
One story says a popular hostess
was assaulted and murdered here.

09:24.080 --> 09:28.380
The hostess made her customers
go into debt to shower her with gifts,

09:28.380 --> 09:31.080
then ghosted them when they ran out of cash.

09:31.750 --> 09:34.670
So a few of them stalked her one night,

09:34.670 --> 09:38.000
and when she got cornered in this phone booth,
she had nowhere left to run...

09:39.670 --> 09:40.500
That's when...

09:42.250 --> 09:44.630
Now, she bears a grudge,

09:44.880 --> 09:47.830
swearing she won't be the only one
to meet such a gruesome end.

09:48.210 --> 09:50.830
Anyone who dares enter or even call this phone booth...

09:51.540 --> 09:55.500
...will meet the same horrific fate!

09:55.920 --> 09:59.500
Wait, how would anyone know
the number of a public pay phone?

09:59.960 --> 10:01.420
Someone posted it online.

10:01.420 --> 10:02.210
Dude!

10:07.920 --> 10:12.290
Whoa, the hell are you doing?! Didn't you hear her?
Going in there is bad news!

10:12.290 --> 10:13.960
You okay? Anything hurt you?!

10:14.080 --> 10:15.000
I didn't see anything.

10:16.830 --> 10:20.130
Her story was pretty convoluted.
Might've just been made up.

10:21.790 --> 10:23.500
This is so stupid...

10:25.580 --> 10:28.130
But the chills I'm getting are the real deal.

10:29.250 --> 10:30.920
Then time for Plan B.

10:30.920 --> 10:31.630
Hello?!

10:31.920 --> 10:33.500
I just told you no!

10:34.500 --> 10:35.500
Give it back.

10:35.500 --> 10:37.460
How are you this strong?!

10:37.460 --> 10:39.000
I can call!

10:39.080 --> 10:40.500
Is anyone listening to me?!

10:40.710 --> 10:42.790
You know this place is dangerous, right?!

10:42.790 --> 10:46.130
Actually, I don't. I can't sense the supernatural.

10:46.130 --> 10:48.000
Eiko, go!

10:49.630 --> 10:52.500
What if something happens to them?!

10:53.290 --> 10:54.210
Dammit!

10:54.830 --> 10:57.920
F-fine, I'll make the call!

10:59.880 --> 11:02.250
And if nothing happens, we're going home!

11:09.960 --> 11:11.040
Help...

11:14.670 --> 11:16.040
Hurry...

11:18.580 --> 11:19.580
Help me...

11:22.670 --> 11:24.080
Hurry...

11:28.750 --> 11:30.380
Hurry...

11:34.130 --> 11:35.710
Wh-what are you...?

11:45.920 --> 11:49.380
OH GOD, OH GOD, OH GOD! IT'S GONNA KILL US!

11:52.670 --> 11:53.500
No.

11:55.290 --> 11:56.540
It killed something else.

12:01.790 --> 12:05.330
What the hell is wrong with this ghost-crazy girl?!

12:05.920 --> 12:07.420
She just thinks ghosts are cool!

12:07.420 --> 12:08.460
I'm just cool, period.

12:09.880 --> 12:13.500
You shouldn't go to these dangerous places!
What would your parents think?!

12:13.960 --> 12:15.130
It's time to start studying!

12:16.960 --> 12:18.210
K..Kei-kun!

12:18.420 --> 12:20.500
When you're done studying, can we talk?

12:21.630 --> 12:23.170
Uh, sure...

12:28.330 --> 12:31.920
I gave her questions from a tough middle school
entrance exam, and she got them all right.

12:32.330 --> 12:36.790
If she's this intelligent,
I shouldn't assume she's just got a screw loose...

12:38.130 --> 12:40.790
Yayoi-chan, you can see those spirits?

12:40.790 --> 12:42.330
I catch them in 4K.

12:43.330 --> 12:44.420
And you like them?

12:44.790 --> 12:46.080
As much as I like plushies.

12:46.710 --> 12:47.500
All done.

12:47.580 --> 12:49.880
Oh, great, thanks.

12:51.000 --> 12:52.540
Back to that phone booth.

12:53.630 --> 12:59.290
The spirit wouldn't come out for me, 
but it did the second you called.

13:00.670 --> 13:04.170
How often do you attract spirits?

13:05.250 --> 13:08.250
If the place is supposed to be haunted?
100 percent of the time.

13:10.380 --> 13:13.460
Okay! Let's see what you can do!

13:13.670 --> 13:14.710
<b>NO</b>

13:17.000 --> 13:18.920
Keitaro, you suck.

13:21.080 --> 13:22.920
Sorry to keep you so late.

13:23.080 --> 13:23.920
It's okay.

13:24.580 --> 13:26.500
So... What's up?

13:28.210 --> 13:31.920
Could you not get so mad at Yayoi-chan?

13:32.210 --> 13:32.960
Huh?

13:33.500 --> 13:36.040
Remember how I said
she started living with me last year?

13:37.170 --> 13:40.380
That's because a year and a half ago,

13:40.580 --> 13:44.670
she lost both her parents in a car accident.

13:46.330 --> 13:48.130
I'm so sorry...

13:48.790 --> 13:51.460
I think the reason she wants to go to haunted places...

13:51.880 --> 13:54.330
...is because she's looking for her mother.

13:54.880 --> 13:55.500
Huh?

13:56.420 --> 13:58.080
<b>Optometrist</b>

13:58.330 --> 14:00.130
We couldn't determine what caused the change,

14:00.330 --> 14:05.210
but from our exam, her double pupils
don't seem to be impairing her vision.

14:05.630 --> 14:08.790
She says she has some kind
of double vision, though. Right?

14:09.170 --> 14:09.830
Uh-huh.

14:11.960 --> 14:16.960
I see normal things and shadowy things.

14:18.830 --> 14:22.290
Well, let's just keep an eye on it and see how things go.

14:37.830 --> 14:38.880
Mommy?

14:39.830 --> 14:42.250
Let's go to the amusement park with Daddy soon!

14:44.000 --> 14:44.790
Okay!

14:48.080 --> 14:51.040
Did you have fun at the amusement park today, Yayoi?

14:51.330 --> 14:53.710
Yeah! Let's go for another round!

14:54.790 --> 14:56.580
Picked up on me saying that, did you?

14:57.500 --> 14:59.670
You do say it a lot, hon.

14:59.880 --> 15:01.040
You got me there...

15:01.750 --> 15:02.500
Daddy...

15:14.920 --> 15:16.130
<b>Shikura Medical Center</b>

15:15.330 --> 15:16.750
Have you heard the story?

15:16.830 --> 15:21.040
<b>YAYOI HOZUKI</b>

15:17.330 --> 15:20.630
You know, the one about the girl in 603,
who lost her parents.

15:21.040 --> 15:23.380
Oh, the head injury?

15:23.630 --> 15:28.080
They tested her cognitive function,
and she scored an IQ of 160...

15:28.380 --> 15:30.170
and it was average before the accident!

15:31.670 --> 15:36.920
I get it now. I used to see two different worlds.

15:38.040 --> 15:39.290
The real world,

15:40.170 --> 15:41.250
and the spirit world.

15:42.380 --> 15:44.330
But after the accident...

15:45.210 --> 15:46.750
...I can see them at the same time!

15:49.000 --> 15:50.290
If that's right...

15:52.960 --> 15:55.460
...then the first thing I saw when I came to...

16:01.500 --> 16:03.130
...was real.

16:04.040 --> 16:06.710
That thing took Mommy away.

16:09.500 --> 16:11.670
<b>HOZUKI FAMILY</b>

16:16.580 --> 16:20.080
I love my Mommy and Daddy.

16:21.630 --> 16:25.130
Just wait a little longer.

16:26.580 --> 16:29.000
I'll bring Mommy home.

16:30.540 --> 16:32.000
I promise.

16:36.790 --> 16:42.540
Yayoi-chan can see spirits,
but she hasn't seen her mom yet.

16:43.790 --> 16:45.210
I think she's lonely.

16:45.420 --> 16:46.540
Yayoi-chan...

16:47.290 --> 16:50.670
This condition made me avoid people for a while, too.

16:51.920 --> 16:54.420
I know I only randomly ended up as her tutor...

16:54.880 --> 16:59.380
...but maybe there's something I can do to help her.

17:10.170 --> 17:12.210
Let's go on a date, Keitaro!

17:12.210 --> 17:15.080
Wow, Yayoi-chan, way to make a move!

17:15.290 --> 17:16.710
Like, right now?!

17:17.880 --> 17:19.790
This is for you.

17:20.750 --> 17:23.540
It will protect you from baddies.

17:24.170 --> 17:25.880
Yayoi-chan...

17:27.380 --> 17:28.330
Wait, the hell is this?!

17:28.330 --> 17:29.250
A jizo statue.

17:29.580 --> 17:31.960
Featuring Eiko's pantyhose.

17:32.500 --> 17:33.960
That she wore yesterday.

17:33.960 --> 17:35.460
Wait, Yayoi-chan!

17:35.710 --> 17:36.580
He took it.

17:37.000 --> 17:38.750
He certainly did...

17:39.330 --> 17:41.210
So where are we going?

17:41.500 --> 17:43.290
You know where!

17:44.380 --> 17:45.540
The same place we went yesterday!

17:45.540 --> 17:46.830
I have eyes!

17:47.130 --> 17:48.790
Why are we here again?!

17:49.460 --> 17:51.170
To see her again.

17:51.460 --> 17:55.830
I called her like crazy but she blocked me. See?

17:57.500 --> 17:59.250
Keitaro, I need your help.

18:01.880 --> 18:03.000
Stay with me.

18:03.460 --> 18:06.500
S-sure, but how am I supposed to help?

18:06.500 --> 18:08.920
Don't be humble. It's watching you now.

18:23.750 --> 18:27.580
Wh-what the hell?! Why won't it open! C'mon!

18:43.000 --> 18:46.130
Help me... Help me!

18:48.080 --> 18:48.920
Kei-kun!

18:53.130 --> 18:56.170
Oh, come on! It's not protecting me at all!

18:56.790 --> 18:58.540
No, it is.

18:58.920 --> 19:02.290
But it's pushing through it anyway.

19:03.460 --> 19:06.670
Just goes to show how badly it wants Keitaro.

19:09.710 --> 19:11.500
Yayoi-chan, what are you doing?!

19:11.500 --> 19:12.460
Don't worry.

19:12.880 --> 19:15.380
This is where I come in.

19:18.330 --> 19:19.670
Yayoi-chan?!

19:19.960 --> 19:21.210
Hang in there, Keitaro.

19:24.080 --> 19:25.460
You must be strong...

19:27.830 --> 19:30.170
...to choose violence over resting in peace.

19:31.380 --> 19:35.330
I'll deliver you unto an endless dream
from which you will never wake.

19:54.500 --> 20:00.170
Don't worry. Keitaro. No matter how tempting you are
to the supernatural, you'll be fine.

20:01.540 --> 20:03.040
Because I'll hunt them all down.

20:12.540 --> 20:17.040
See, everything's fine! You made it out of there alive!

20:17.210 --> 20:18.750
What part of this is fine?!

20:19.380 --> 20:22.420
I really thought I was gonna die there, you know!

20:22.630 --> 20:24.330
But you didn't.

20:25.750 --> 20:28.830
You'll be here tomorrow.

20:29.790 --> 20:31.040
Yayoi-chan...

20:33.630 --> 20:38.580
Wait, why do I still feel really creeped out?

20:42.380 --> 20:44.040
<b>OMIKI</b>

20:52.710 --> 20:55.580
Kei-kun! Thanks for all your hard work today!

20:57.080 --> 21:00.960
All that just reminded me how much
I hate dealing with the supernatural.

21:02.080 --> 21:04.330
You can't fool me, Kei-kun.

21:04.330 --> 21:06.460
Huh? What's that mean?

21:06.790 --> 21:08.630
You just have to admit it to yourself.

21:09.170 --> 21:11.420
Really think back on what happened...

21:12.130 --> 21:14.580
Because I saw it again yesterday.

21:15.540 --> 21:18.290
Fine, I'll make the call!

21:19.040 --> 21:25.880
You said one thing, but your actions
betrayed how you really felt inside.

21:29.790 --> 21:30.830
Kei-kun...

21:33.000 --> 21:35.670
...you love to feel fear.

21:38.000 --> 21:40.250
N-no way...

21:41.830 --> 21:43.460
I'm trying to change.

21:44.420 --> 21:46.420
But those words caught me in their web.

21:47.040 --> 21:48.880
As if to shake them off, I asked...

21:49.130 --> 21:53.170
Yayoi-chan! Please tell me
you don't want to go back there.

21:53.170 --> 21:54.710
Don't need to.

21:55.960 --> 21:57.670
Nothing's there anymore.

21:58.130 --> 21:58.960
Huh?

21:59.080 --> 22:00.790
Even if you went, nothing would show.

22:02.790 --> 22:05.080
That leaves one question.

22:06.460 --> 22:11.670
If Yayoi is so spiritually sensitive,
why does she have so much trouble finding spirits?

22:13.040 --> 22:14.670
If I had to guess...

22:14.460 --> 22:16.420
<b>Yayoi</b>

22:15.500 --> 22:16.250
Maybe...

22:20.580 --> 22:25.710
...the spirits themselves are trying their best to avoid her.

22:26.880 --> 22:27.750
Kodoku.

22:28.330 --> 22:31.460
"Kodoku"? You mean, like, the word for "lonely"?

22:31.670 --> 22:32.500
No.

22:35.130 --> 22:39.750
Kodoku is made by putting lots of poisonous bugs
in a jar and letting them fight.

22:40.380 --> 22:44.920
Whatever survives gets made into poison
to curse someone else.

22:47.210 --> 22:49.420
I have lots of friends.

22:50.380 --> 22:55.540
O-oh. Well, if you ever need anything, just ask, okay?

22:57.670 --> 22:59.920
The cherry blossoms, painted with moonlight,

23:01.000 --> 23:04.420
reflected in her haunted eyes, seemed to pull me in,

23:04.880 --> 23:08.210
beckoning to me, drawing me ever closer.

23:10.330 --> 23:12.380
That spring would forever be etched into my memory...

23:13.330 --> 23:18.290
...as the season where she and I came to meet.

23:22.290 --> 23:28.330
To exorcise the curse plaguing his hand,
Keitaro heads to the shrine headed by his grandmother.

23:29.040 --> 23:35.380
But in that sacred location, his affliction seems to attract
beings that are even more ghastly.
